# Generated from: specs/bug-fix-canonical-umbrella-classification-for-verified-specs/requirements.md
# Issue: #159
# Type: Defect regression

@regression @issue-159
Feature: Canonical umbrella classification accepts verified specifications
  Canonical umbrella classification previously rejected the lifecycle-owned verification report
  and allowed one invalid candidate to suppress unrelated targeted or audit results.
  The classifier now recognizes verified trees while preserving strict validation and isolated diagnostics.

  @regression
  Scenario: Accept a verified umbrella specification in every classifier mode
    Given a multi-PR feature-spec tree contains the four required regular authoring blobs plus a regular verification-report.md
    When parent, publication, and audit mode validate that tree
    Then the verification report is not classified as an unexpected entry
    And each mode reaches the status supported by the umbrella evidence
    And exact tree identity includes the verification report

  @regression
  Scenario: Reject every unrecognized or unsafe spec-tree shape
    Given a candidate spec tree is missing a required authoring file, contains a symlink, or contains an unrecognized entry
    When a classifier mode validates the tree
    Then validation fails closed with a stable path-specific reason
    And the helper does not mutate the worktree, index, refs, remote state, or GitHub

  @regression
  Scenario: Ignore an unrelated invalid candidate during targeted parent lookup
    Given bounded refs contain an invalid candidate unrelated to requested parent issue 159 and a valid candidate for issue 159
    When parent mode queries issue 159
    Then the unrelated candidate does not change or suppress the valid parent result
    And malformed or ambiguous evidence that claims issue 159 still fails closed with scoped diagnostics

  @regression
  Scenario: Retain valid findings in a mixed repository audit
    Given bounded refs contain valid, invalid, canonical, stranded, divergent, and ambiguous umbrella candidates
    When repository audit mode runs with JSON output
    Then valid per-spec findings are retained
    And candidate-specific validation gaps are reported without aborting the audit
    And a systemic Git, default-branch, or bounded-ref failure still makes the audit unverifiable

  @regression
  Scenario: Continue child implementation from a verified canonical baseline without resealing
    Given a verified umbrella spec is canonical on the refreshed default branch and a feature child has an approved child-scoped amendment
    When write-spec completes for the child and write-code begins
    Then no child-numbered seal commit or second umbrella publication pull request is created
    And the next-step output points to write-code
    And the write-code parent gate accepts the canonical parent baseline and loads the child-amended specification
    And the child branch tree is not required to equal the parent baseline tree

  @regression
  Scenario: Preserve the complete canonical umbrella lifecycle from issue 157
    Given the issue 157 publication, recovery, divergence, ambiguity, symlink, idempotency, and no-mutation regressions
    When the lifecycle adds canonical merge, implementation verification, a later child amendment, and write-code handoff
    Then every classifier mode and consumer handoff passes with verification-report.md present
    And exact publication scope, default-branch precedence, idempotency, symlink rejection, and read-only behavior remain unchanged
